From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:28:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: a held station's txq back when tx_queue_skb()
 fails

In mt76_txq_schedule_list(), the branch for a station the driver holds
(dozing, PS buffering in the hardware) returned on an error from
mt76_txq_send_burst() without giving the txq back to mac80211, unlike
the awake branch. The frame tx_queue_skb() failed on (no token, no
txwi, a DMA mapping error) was dropped there with its airtime released,
so nothing of the station was in flight to re-arm it either: the rest of
its frames stayed off the active list, none in the firmware to set its
TIM bit, until new traffic for that TID came or the station woke by
itself.

Give the txq back, and schedule the worker again: no completion and
nothing from a dozing station will. Each failure drops a frame, so this
ends.

The power save simulation's failure cases found it (a later commit).
Reported by a Gemini review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tx.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index cd3f8dd8..497da7b3 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -682,8 +682,19 @@ mt76_txq_schedule_list(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_txq_id qid)
 			if (!mt76_txq_stopped(q))
 				n_frames = mt76_txq_send_burst(phy, q, mtxq, wcid);
 
-			if (unlikely(n_frames < 0))
+			/*
+			 * The frame tx_queue_skb() failed on was dropped, its
+			 * airtime released: no completion will re-arm this
+			 * station (mt76_tx_ps_rearm()), and a dozing one sends
+			 * nothing to wake us either. Back on the list, and the
+			 * worker comes round again (each failure drops a frame,
+			 * so this ends).
+			 */
+			if (unlikely(n_frames < 0)) {
+				ieee80211_return_txq(phy->hw, txq, false);
+				mt76_worker_schedule(&dev->tx_worker);
 				return n_frames;
+			}
 
 			/*
 			 * Keep the station in the airtime scheduler only while it
